      "math_academy_id": "e-10994",
      "problem": "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B),$ where \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14123092/assets/3e712748e8fc744fc15cd6d7c1549aaba236b3254d9c65289288133e5daefad4.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14123092/assets/0a19cbfc3164a365bb02386d16bac01562a36b39de41a4b2909e4397684f2cac.svg)\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24.$",
